  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of the Interior obligated $53.3M in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Interior processed 701 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $76K. The Department of the Interior's obligations are down 99.2% year over year, a sharp drop compared with prior fiscal years that reported multibillion-dollar totals. The Department of the Interior obligated $6.8B in FY26, $6.6B in FY25, $8.1B in FY24, $7.6B in FY23, and $6.5B in FY22. The Department of the Interior's spending in FY2027 to date concentrates in a few categories, led by Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction at $20.3M and Computer Systems Design Services at $9.3M. The Department of the Interior's top contractors for FY2027 to date include NW CONSTRUCTION, INC with $11.7M and MANTECH ADVANCED SYSTEMS INTERNATIONAL, INC. with $7.9M. The Department of the Interior's current-year totals are partial because figures are contract obligations and fiscal year totals are still in progress.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with recent years?",
        "body": "The Department of the Interior obligated $53.3M in FY2027 to date, compared with $6.8B in FY26 and $8.1B in FY24. The Department of the Interior's obligations are down 99.2% year over year. The Department of the Interior recorded 701 awards so far in FY2027, with an average award size of $76K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is Interior spending concentrated this fiscal year?",
        "body": "Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction leads Interior spending at $20.3M, followed by Computer Systems Design Services at $9.3M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $5.3M. The Department of the Interior also obligated funds for Support Activities for Forestry ($4.9M), Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation ($4.8M), and Facilities Support Services ($2.1M)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of the Interior spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior obligated $53.3M in contracts in FY2027 to date. The Department of the Interior recorded 701 awards this fiscal year to date and the average award size was $76K. The Department of the Interior's obligations are down 99.2% year over year. The Department of the Interior's prior fiscal year totals were $6.8B in FY26, $6.6B in FY25, $8.1B in FY24, $7.6B in FY23, and $6.5B in FY22."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Interior buy?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior buys construction, IT, research, forestry support, and air transport services. The Department of the Interior's top NAICS categories in FY2027 to date are Other Heavy and Civil Engineering Construction ($20.3M), Computer Systems Design Services ($9.3M), Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) ($5.3M), Support Activities for Forestry ($4.9M), and Nonscheduled Chartered Passenger Air Transportation ($4.8M). The Department of the Interior also obligated funds for Facilities Support Services ($2.1M), Nonscheduled Chartered Freight Air Transportation ($2M), Environmental Consulting Services ($1.9M), Software Publishers ($1.1M), and Support Activities for Animal Production ($844K)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Interior's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The Department of the Interior's largest contractors in FY2027 to date are NW CONSTRUCTION, INC ($11.7M), MANTECH ADVANCED SYSTEMS INTERNATIONAL, INC. ($7.9M), and HSG PARK JOINT VENTURE 3, LLC ($7.5M). The Department of the Interior also obligated funds to BRIDGER AEROSPACE GROUP, LLC ($5.2M), VANTOR SERVICES INC. ($4.4M), HENRYS AERIAL SERVICE INC ($2.6M), AERO SPRAY INC ($2.3M), DIDLAKE INC ($1.5M), TIMBERLINE HELICOPTERS INC ($1.2M), and KOKOSING CONSTRUCTION COMPANY, INC. ($1.1M)."
    }
